{
  "run_id": "PMC12941970__expert_context__web_trend_focus_ground_b_o3mini__s2",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The starting material is a conventional coarse-grained bulk CoCrFeNi alloy without tailored surface modifications.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Physical vapor deposition can produce the proposed graded, adaptive nanolayer on CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The graded nanolayer will remain adherent and mechanically robust at low temperatures.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12019924::web::009::tribological_performance_of_2d_hea"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperatures, the nanolayer will undergo controlled oxidation or another nanophase transformation to create a lubricious surface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12019924::web::003::main",
        "PMC7311485::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nanolayer-induced surface hardening will improve low-temperature wear resistance.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8470387::web::011::3_3_high_temperature_friction_and_wear_p"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Improved coating adhesion will reduce wear at low temperatures.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing temperature and sliding-induced shear will activate the coating transformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12019924::web::003::main",
        "PMC7311485::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The transformed oxide layers or nanoflakes will lower interfacial shear strength and thereby reduce friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12019924::web::003::main"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The transformed surface phase will act as a protective layer and reduce wear at high temperatures.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8470387::web::011::3_3_high_temperature_friction_and_wear_p"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to unmodified CoCrFeNi, the coated material will have lower friction throughout approximately 25–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12019924::web::003::main",
        "PMC7311485::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC8470387::web::011::3_3_high_temperature_friction_and_wear_p"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to unmodified CoCrFeNi, the coated material will have a lower wear rate throughout approximately 25–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12019924::web::003::main",
        "PMC12019924::web::009::tribological_performance_of_2d_hea",
        "PMC7311485::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC8470387::web::011::3_3_high_temperature_friction_and_wear_p"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The friction and wear improvements will persist as contact load varies over the range typical of tribological tests.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12019924::web::003::main",
        "PMC12019924::web::009::tribological_performance_of_2d_hea"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coating will improve tribological performance in both inert and mildly oxidizing environments.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12019924::web::003::main",
        "PMC7311485::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unmodified CoCrFeNi typically develops increased friction and wear variability with temperature, especially when uncontrolled oxidation or phase changes occur.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coating's performance may be compromised under extremely high loads or highly aggressive oxidative conditions.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
